---
const ranges = [
  ['Early SaaS', '$300–$3,000/month', 'Avoidable support, founder time, failed activation, repeated explanation.'],
  ['Small SaaS', '$2,000–$15,000/month', 'Support load, onboarding drag, bad data, qualification noise.'],
  ['Medium SaaS', '$10,000–$75,000/month', 'Product, Support, Customer Success, Onboarding and Implementation carrying the same missing scaffold.'],
  ['Larger mid-market systems', '$50,000+/month', 'Activation, retention, implementation timelines or multiple teams affected.'],
];
---

<section id="cost-of-inaction">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-label">Cost of Inaction</div>
    <h2>The cost is already being paid. Usually under the wrong line item.</h2>
    <div class="cost-range-grid">
      {ranges.map(([label, amount, detail]) => (
        <div class="project-card cost-range-card">
          <div class="cred-institution">{label}</div>
          <h3>{amount}</h3>
          <p class="project-body">{detail}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="section-copy cost-transfer-close">
      These ranges are not promises. They are a way to ask the right question: is the recurring
      cost of not diagnosing the flow already higher than the cost of the review?
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
